<pre class=metadata>
Title: The Relation Attribute
Shortname: relation-attribute
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/HTML-Additions/relation-attribute/spec/
Repository: arronei/HTML-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification extends HTML with a <code>relation</code> content attribute for
    <{input}> elements in the Checkbox state. It relates checkboxes that share a name. With
    <code>relation="parent"</code>, one checkbox controls the others: checking it checks them all,
    and it shows whether none, some, or all of them are checked, using the indeterminate state for
    "some". With <code>relation="linked"</code>, checkboxes mirror each other, so checking one checks
    them all. Both work without script.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

